00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.580
GANG CHEN: OK.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.040
Hope you had all a good weekend.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.660
It was very lovely.

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:33.750
We had a lot of fun
during the weekend.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.390
So recall what we were
talking the last lecture.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.160
We discussed the
Maxwell equations.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.910
Electric field-- this is a,
say, very magnetic field,

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.100
general electric field.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.470
Current generate magnetic
field, and what Maxwell added

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:59.370
is the displacement field that,
say, the time derivative also

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.380
generate magnetic field.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:05.940
So this setup for equations
from the Maxwell equation.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:12.450
And one comment I
thought I forgot to make

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.560
is this is actually called
macroscopic Maxwell equation.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.620
And you can write
atomic Maxwell equation

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.930
that does not involve
the displacement,

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:34.650
because displacement,
recall, is the polarization

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.800
due to external field plus
external field together.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:46.620
It's the response of the
atoms to the external field.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.760
And similarly,
magnetic induction

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:56.020
also includes magnetic moment
and, say, magnetic field.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:59.430
So the atomic Maxwell
equation, actually, you

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:04.500
can go to write without
those, say, D and B.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.900
But you have to sum
up overall atoms.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.820
And you do not use the
concept dielectric constant.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.910
And this is, in fact, the
area that we're currently

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.760
trying to work on to bridge--

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.940
to build a bridge between
the heat conduction

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.610
and electromagnetic wave.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:27.100
Because we're doing an
experiment when two surface is

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.420
really, really close--

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.050
like 1 nanometer close--

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:34.050
originally we're
using the macroscopic

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.340
of Maxwell equation.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.550
But in this regime,
we're no longer--

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:42.340
we're questioning whether
that's valid or not.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:48.180
So by coming back from this
set of macroscopic Maxwell

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:53.640
equations, we can find
a plane wave solution

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.680
for the wave propagating
in a homogeneous media.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:05.100
A homogeneous media means
I have the permeability

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.780
and permitivity--

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:11.730
permitivity and permeability
independent of space.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.780
So it's a function of
frequency, but it's

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.820
independent of free space.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:20.550
And in this case,
the wave vector,

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.050
when we substitute
back into the equation,

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:26.460
we find the wave vector
is related to frequency.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:30.960
That's a dispersion relation
through the permitivity

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.780
and permeability, which
when we will normalize

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:38.310
to vacuum values, we have the
relative dielectric constant

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:43.950
and the relative
magnetic permeability.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.040
And so this is the square.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.940
So if I take the magnitude
of the wave vector--

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.770
right, this is vector--

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.980
magnitude of wave vector,
I can write this equation

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.120
in terms of omega.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.240
And omega equals CK.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:03.240
That's what you're familiar
with for free space.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.650
Right?

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.570
See the wavelength
times frequency

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:07.680
equals speed of light.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.420
That's what it gives.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.730
And this N is the refractive
index, the optical constant

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.440
of the material.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.230
And different material have
different optical constant.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:22.170
But it's not a constant.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.360
And it's very
frequency-dependent.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:29.110
So it's a misnomer.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.000
So if you take the
derivative of N--

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.880
normally we take only
the positive root.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.110
So most of the case,
don't worry about it.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.360
It's a positive root.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.710
Refractive index equals square
root dielectric constant

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:48.840
and relative magnetic
permeability.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:54.000
And but in optical frequency
range, this is one usually.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.740
So it's really just the square
root of dielectric constant.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.970
And because this one could
be including imaginary part,

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.390
so when you take
a rood, generally

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:09.060
your optical constant
have a real part

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.190
and an imaginary part.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:14.250
And the imaginary
part is associated,

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.850
particularly epsilon r, the
imaginary part associated

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.810
with the loss.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.230
And correspondingly,
this kappa, which

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.630
we call extinction
coefficient, is

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:29.350
also associated with loss,
the damping of the wave

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:33.450
when it propagates
through the medium.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.620
And we said, if you
check, basically these

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:41.520
are all characteristics you
can derive from the equation,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.910
this plane wave solution.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:46.830
And if you plug in plane wave
solution, you find that this E.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.050
You can also use
that to find the H.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:53.400
The E is perpendicular
to H. So that's--

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.640
the two fields are
perpendicular to each other.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:01.140
And it's perpendicular to
the direction of propagation.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:06.000
And that's why electromagnetic
wave is a transverse way.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.700
It's perpendicular to the
direction of propagation.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:12.570
And also, normally it's
a right-handed wave

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:18.330
because it's E cross H
gives you the K direction.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.850
And that's when you
take the square root

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:23.370
as a positive and
negative square root

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.010
is just a recent invention.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.500
The theory was there, but
let's say it was really--

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.690
it's a [INAUDIBLE]
field that is based

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.460
on designing
artificial structures

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:37.840
so that when both epsilon
the mil are negative,

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:41.290
you should take a
negative square root.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.150
We commented that at
end of last lecture.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:46.960
So this where we were.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:53.120
It's basically giving
you the vector equations.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:56.650
And if you recall, before this
we're looking at the electron.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:59.470
It's not-- it's a scalar wave.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:03.130
We're looking at the electron
reflection as a potential step.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:07.090
So we give a reflectance and
transmittance at the interface.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:10.120
And where we're going
is doing the same thing.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:14.500
I have electromagnetic wave
comes towards the interface.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.450
What's the corresponding
reflectance?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.700
What corresponding
transmittance?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:24.100
And similarly, after that
we go to acoustic wave.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:27.490
And acoustic wave is a more
complicated [INAUDIBLE] wave

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:30.250
because it has
three polarization--

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:33.670
longitudinal, which is
the same as the K vector,

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:36.250
vibration direction,
and two transverse.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:39.910
So that is even
more complicated.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:43.780
But we're going to at least
give you some idea of those.

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:46.240
Oh, different waves
actually behave,

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.050
from wave perspective,
actually, very similarly

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:52.430
in terms of the behavior.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:55.330
So let's continue.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.380
And what we want first
is a further look

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:02.070
at the wave propagation
in homogeneous medium.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:18.820
And if you use the
Maxwell equation,

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:20.800
this is what you can prove.

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.890
And I'm not going
to write the mass

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.600
because it's a very involving.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.060
I mean write vector.

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.640
Let me just point out--

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:33.159
so when you use Maxwell
equation, what you can,

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:36.289
do you can multiply
H to this equation.

00:08:36.289 --> 00:08:38.980
What do you see,
B is mu H, right?

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.500
So that's 1/2 mu H square.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:45.980
That's like the magnetic
field energy, stored energy.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:49.330
And if you multiply
this by E, and what

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:55.120
you have here is a epsilon,
say, D is epsilon E, right?

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.600
So you get 1/2 half
epsilon E squared.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.660
That's the electrical
field energy stored.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.610
And when you add
them in together,

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:06.790
the left-hand side
will give you the rate

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:09.490
of change of energy
stored in the system,

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:11.710
if you take it any
system and you apply it.

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.810
And the right-hand
should be the flux

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:17.080
that's going across
the system boundaries.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:20.620
So that's the interpretation
if you do your math operation.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:24.010
And what you find
out is then that flux

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:27.310
of energy going across
the system boundary

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:31.870
gives you the energy flux
of electromagnetic wave.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.355
And this is the Poynting vector.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:49.030
Poynting vector
is E cross H. So E

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:54.710
cross H is the energy
propagation direction.

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:55.790
OK?

00:09:55.790 --> 00:10:01.710
And if you think about my
electric field is varying

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.810
as a function of omega t.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:09.810
So the instantaneously
my S, the energy flux--

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.390
right-- Poynting vector
gives me the energy flux.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:22.380
I should not say the energy--

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.925
really should be power flux.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:33.390
And what I have here is the--

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:40.580
it is a function of
2 omega, timewise.

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:42.210
Right?

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.940
Because if you look at
the E, it's I omega.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:49.470
And if you have 2 sine omega
times each other, omega T

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:52.860
times each other,
you get 2 omega t.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:57.000
So the energy--
the power flux here

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.360
is a rapid changing
function with time.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.580
Because the frequency
of light, visible light

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:07.540
at least, is 10 to the 14 hertz.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:13.810
So 2 omega will give you
even much faster, right?

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:18.070
So in this case,
normally we don't care.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:19.690
We can't measure.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:25.130
We cannot measure the
instantaneous power here.

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:27.950
And what we measure
is time average power.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.430
So if you go to do
your time average--

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:41.620
time average-- and no
proof, but it's much easier

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:44.170
if you calculate this way.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.150
It's the equivalent.

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:50.860
It's E cross H
complex conjugate.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:56.440
And if you go to think about the
mass flux from the Schrodinger

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:04.930
equation, we wrote it as also
real part of a [INAUDIBLE]

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:08.890
and a grading of a
complex conjugate, right?

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:13.240
So you see the similarity
between these different flux.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:19.180
I'm writing this as a E
cross H complex conjugate.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:25.450
So all this, say, this is a
time average Poynting vector.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:29.770
And now let's look at if I
have the plane wave propagating

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:33.550
inside a medium,
how it will change,

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:37.880
how the Poynting vector
change as a function of space.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:41.050
So let's say I
have a plane wave,

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:44.260
and I'm careful
taking my coordinate.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:45.820
This is z direction.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.130
That's the direction
of propagation.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.100
And this is the E direction.

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:54.400
It's in the x, so xy.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:59.500
So y, then say, I would
expect my magnetic field will

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:04.900
be pointing E cross H,
gives me A, pointing out.

00:13:08.310 --> 00:13:10.560
But you can prove it.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:21.780
You can use your E. Let's say my
electric field in the Ex omega

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:28.430
t, so it's the x component--

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:31.240
electric field pointing
to x direction only.

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:34.530
And the magnitude of
the electrical field

00:13:34.530 --> 00:13:42.300
times the exponential minus I.
And if you replace K relation

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:47.550
here, what we have,
K equals omega C0 N.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.770
So I can take out the omega.

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:59.160
So omega t minus N C0 times z.

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:05.250
This is writing my plane wave
for electrical field polarized

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:08.970
in the x direction,
propagating in the z direction.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:16.450
So from here, if I know
Ex, I can go back here

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:18.400
because I don't know H, right?

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:22.550
I say that H is a function, is
only in the Y direction only.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:27.670
And in fact, you can use the
Maxwell equation to prove it.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:32.120
So to find the H, I use
the first equation, right?

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:36.690
The curve for electrical field.

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:45.890
So I can say here, what I
have is a univector x, y, z

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:51.950
And have D Dx, D, Dy, and D, Dz.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:00.810
So this is for
calculating the curve.

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:08.590
And I have Ex, so
x component only--

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.160
Ex 0 0.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:21.220
That's the left-hand side
of the first equation.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:26.200
And the Ex is a
function of z, remember.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.540
Ex is just a vector direction.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:32.110
It's not a function of
x It's a function of z,

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.270
if you look at here.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:40.940
On the right-hand side,
I have B. B is mu, so D--

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:43.270
so mu DH Dt.

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:48.100
So I have DHx Dt.

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.230
And this is the x direction--

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:58.120
DHy Dt y direction,
DHz Dt z direction.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.520
Right?

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:05.560
So I'm writing out the
first equation there--

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:06.060
vector.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.070
OK.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.580
And now if you
look at it, I said

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:16.220
this is a function
of z time z only.

00:16:16.220 --> 00:16:21.000
So it's only a
function of z and time.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.920
So if I take a derivative
of this, I-- of course,

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.580
the x component-- so
x, I take out this.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:30.590
I have all 0.

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:31.580
Right?

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:33.635
So that means actually Hx is 0.

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:40.420
Hx is 0.

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:46.330
And then if I look at the
z component, here, here--

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:51.040
so Dz-- D0 Dx is 0.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:56.860
DEx Dy-- but the Ex
is function of z only.

00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:59.470
So that's also 0.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.570
So I have Hz0.

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:06.160
So this will validate
what we're talking.

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:07.930
It's a transverse wave.

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:11.609
And H is perpendicular to E.

00:17:11.609 --> 00:17:15.450
I only have the second
term, the y term--

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:18.990
DHy Dt, because
the y, if I say--

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:22.720
look at this, a vector.

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:24.210
So I take these two out.

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:27.770
So I have this 0--

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:28.940
D0 Dx.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.000
And then I have DEx Dz.

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.990
This one is not 0.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:35.590
Right?

00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:46.480
So I have really minus
mu DHy Dt equals minus--

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:50.350
this is the second term on the
first row, so my sign is minus.

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:52.880
And then I have--
this is a positive,

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:59.760
this is negative--
is minus D Dx Dz.

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:02.200
Right?

00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:04.190
So I know my Ex.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:06.620
I have given my Ex DEx Dz.

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:09.370
I take out the derivative.

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:12.480
I integrate it with
respect to time.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.060
I get my Hy.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:15.990
Right?

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:19.260
So let me write down Hy.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:23.160
In this case what do
you get, without going

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.740
through the intermediate steps--

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:43.180
my Hy component is E0 times
N mu C0 and exponential

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:51.160
minus I omega t
minus N C0 times z.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:57.950
So again, it's a wave
propagating in the z direction.

00:18:57.950 --> 00:19:00.800
And it's only y
direction component

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:05.300
is now 0, so it's perpendicular
to the electrical field.

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:10.080
And in fact, if you
look at E0 times this,

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:15.160
essentially is my Ex, right?

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:22.350
E0 times this exponential factor
is my Ex, not the vector, just

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:25.000
the form in the x direction.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:31.920
So in fact, let me use
this right at the N--

00:19:31.920 --> 00:19:36.480
mu 0 C0 times Ex.

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:39.600
But, say, this is
the magnitude of Ex

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:43.300
is not vector Ex
because the component is

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:46.030
in the y direction.

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:48.670
OK?

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:52.240
So that's Hy.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:57.380
When I do my Poynting vector, I
will need all three components,

00:19:57.380 --> 00:20:00.490
so that's why I'm writing out.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:06.760
And in fact, what if you
have a positive sign--

00:20:06.760 --> 00:20:09.910
rather than negative--
that's a forward propagating.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:14.900
If you have a
backward propagating,

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:20.790
and your corresponding sign here
in the front will also change.

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:24.020
And you'll have, in
that case, you'll have

00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:31.310
Hy equals negative N mu C0--

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:35.690
mu 0 C0 and Exy.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:39.620
And this is for a negative
propagating wave, a sign

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:40.550
change.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:45.260
And that's understandable
because what I have here,

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.940
this is the
propagation direction.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:48.630
I said it's a right-hand wave.

00:20:48.630 --> 00:20:51.260
So E cross H is pointing out.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:54.350
But now if the wave goes
the other direction,

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.840
H will pointing in
the opposite direction

00:20:56.840 --> 00:20:58.100
to form my right-hand wave.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:08.510
And I commented, when
both E and, I say,

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:16.750
mu and epsilon are negative,
you have to do your left-hand.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.260
And if you look
at this, here Hy--

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:25.650
if mu is negative, that changes
direction, real direction,

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:27.950
of the magnetic field.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:30.370
And similarly, if
epsilon is negative,

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:31.700
that change the real direction.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:38.260
So the negative root is actually
of this refractive index here,

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:43.210
is actually the requirement from
the Maxwell equation itself.

00:21:43.210 --> 00:21:47.550
There's no-- it's just
a math requirement.

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:51.930
So it was the first pointed
out by this Russian scientist,

00:21:51.930 --> 00:21:56.880
[INAUDIBLE],, if both the
epsilon and mu are negative,

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:59.760
you should take
the negative root.

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:06.110
But the nature of
materials all have, say,

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:08.220
epsilon mu pretty
close to vacuum.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:12.300
So if the mu r is 1,
so normally people

00:22:12.300 --> 00:22:18.610
say that's just an academic
exercise until, in the '90s,

00:22:18.610 --> 00:22:21.510
people start to actually
make artificial structure

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:23.410
have a magnetic resonance.

00:22:23.410 --> 00:22:27.300
So the magnetic response resists
the external magnetic field.

00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:29.580
And that could
generate a negative mu.

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:32.640
And in this case, when
you can design material

00:22:32.640 --> 00:22:36.870
with both epsilon and mu
negative together and become

00:22:36.870 --> 00:22:39.380
negative.

00:22:39.380 --> 00:22:43.770
So I am not done yet.

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:45.530
I have my Ex.

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:47.330
I have my Hy.

00:22:47.330 --> 00:22:51.470
And I can go calculate
Poynting vector.

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:53.515
So let's calculate
the Poynting vector.

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:00.220
So this is the complexity
with the vector waves,

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:04.310
so you have to do always
a vector operation.

00:23:04.310 --> 00:23:11.160
If you look at your Poynting
vector, and at the end,

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:15.230
you'll find out this
is only z component.

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:19.160
There's no x, y
component because your Ex

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:22.940
is in the x direction,
and the H is y direction.

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:26.840
And the cross product is
only in the z direction.

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:31.850
So let me skip that the
vector form and just say,

00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:35.180
this is the time average
vector in the z direction--

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:48.100
is 1/2 real part of E, now
Ex Hy complex conjugate.

00:23:48.100 --> 00:23:50.740
And this is what you get if
you write all these three

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:54.380
components, and you only have
the z direction component.

00:23:54.380 --> 00:24:00.460
So now I can plug in Ex and Hy.

00:24:04.820 --> 00:24:07.130
And you have to be careful
of this N refractive

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:11.240
index or optical constant, has
both real and imagined part.

00:24:11.240 --> 00:24:14.030
So when I take a
complex conjugate,

00:24:14.030 --> 00:24:15.740
this one I take complex.

00:24:15.740 --> 00:24:17.390
This one I take complex.

00:24:17.390 --> 00:24:19.970
This I I take inverse.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:23.510
And this N, I have to
take complex conjugate.

00:24:23.510 --> 00:24:25.040
So you have to do all that.

00:24:25.040 --> 00:24:28.550
And you see, I omega
t minus I omega t,

00:24:28.550 --> 00:24:30.530
because of plus I omega t.

00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:33.320
So I omega t cancel.

00:24:33.320 --> 00:24:38.570
E is negative I omega t because
that's last year-- because I,

00:24:38.570 --> 00:24:40.610
actually, I was
doing time averages.

00:24:40.610 --> 00:24:42.480
Time should not be there.

00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:44.980
So this always cancels time.

00:24:44.980 --> 00:24:54.450
And so what I have then
is a 1/2 real part of E0.

00:24:54.450 --> 00:24:56.280
That's the electrical field.

00:24:56.280 --> 00:25:01.500
And the exponential
negative negative

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:08.550
is a positive N. And C0
times z, that the first Ex--

00:25:08.550 --> 00:25:19.100
Hy is E0 complex conjugate
N complex conjugate Dy

00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:21.680
by mu 0 C0.

00:25:21.680 --> 00:25:26.220
And I take mu is pretty
much as in vacuum.

00:25:26.220 --> 00:25:33.140
And then I have an exponential,
and this becomes a plus I.

00:25:33.140 --> 00:25:38.150
And this is a negative, so I
have exponential negative N

00:25:38.150 --> 00:25:41.619
complex conjugate C0 z.

00:25:45.371 --> 00:25:48.490
That my Poynting vector.

00:25:48.490 --> 00:25:49.630
Right?

00:25:49.630 --> 00:25:50.780
So what you have--

00:25:50.780 --> 00:25:53.590
electric field,
complex conjugate--

00:25:53.590 --> 00:25:56.280
that's just a magnitude.

00:25:56.280 --> 00:25:57.660
These are real.

00:25:57.660 --> 00:25:59.160
Now here I have to be careful.

00:25:59.160 --> 00:26:00.390
It's the real part only.

00:26:00.390 --> 00:26:02.840
Imaginary part drops out.

00:26:02.840 --> 00:26:10.870
And these 2 exponential is
N minus N complex conjugate.

00:26:10.870 --> 00:26:12.860
That gives me 2 I kappa.

00:26:15.620 --> 00:26:19.730
2 I kappa-- oh, I forgot,
there is another I omega.

00:26:19.730 --> 00:26:21.960
I omega should multiply in.

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:26.020
So I actually have I omega.

00:26:26.020 --> 00:26:28.660
I have I omega, right?

00:26:28.660 --> 00:26:33.700
So N complex only give
me 2 I kappa times

00:26:33.700 --> 00:26:36.730
this another I,
actually is real.

00:26:36.730 --> 00:26:39.820
So here N is real.

00:26:39.820 --> 00:26:43.570
Here is the imaginary
part in the exponent.

00:26:43.570 --> 00:26:50.520
So what I have then
is 1/2 E0 squared

00:26:50.520 --> 00:26:56.730
and mu 0 C0 and
the real part, N,

00:26:56.730 --> 00:27:05.760
and exponential minus
4 pi kappa over lambda.

00:27:05.760 --> 00:27:08.310
And this lambda is
lambda in vacuum.

00:27:08.310 --> 00:27:12.910
I have used, say,
omega C0, right?

00:27:12.910 --> 00:27:18.420
Omega over C0 equals
2 pi over lambda.

00:27:18.420 --> 00:27:20.640
So I substitute this in.

00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:27.290
And that's how the Poynting
vector in a homogeneous media

00:27:27.290 --> 00:27:34.310
of refractive index N kappa is
changing in the z direction.

00:27:34.310 --> 00:27:35.882
Here is z.

00:27:35.882 --> 00:27:40.260
It's exponential
decay function, right?

00:27:40.260 --> 00:27:47.320
That decaying exponent, alpha,
is 4 pi kappa over lambda.

00:27:47.320 --> 00:27:49.140
This is absorption coefficient.

00:28:03.450 --> 00:28:06.390
And the inverse of this
absorption coefficient

00:28:06.390 --> 00:28:08.460
is sometimes called
the skin depth.

00:28:08.460 --> 00:28:09.750
So if the inverse--

00:28:09.750 --> 00:28:11.080
that's a depth.

00:28:11.080 --> 00:28:17.820
So you can see, when z equals
that skin depth inverse, delta

00:28:17.820 --> 00:28:20.580
equals 1 over alpha.

00:28:20.580 --> 00:28:25.050
When z equals delta,
we have the field

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:27.210
the decay to
exponential minus 1.

00:28:30.970 --> 00:28:33.970
So what did we learn here?

00:28:33.970 --> 00:28:37.390
You can say that when
electromagnetic field is

00:28:37.390 --> 00:28:45.340
propagating in a lossy media,
kappa is now 0, the field decay

00:28:45.340 --> 00:28:46.940
exponentially.

00:28:46.940 --> 00:28:54.430
And that's the electromagnetic
wave is absorbed by the medium.

00:28:54.430 --> 00:28:59.830
And in fact, this
is very important

00:28:59.830 --> 00:29:03.010
when you make solar cells.

00:29:03.010 --> 00:29:07.320
This determine how
deep the photon

00:29:07.320 --> 00:29:09.540
penetrate into the material.

00:29:09.540 --> 00:29:14.310
And silicon is an
indirect-gap semiconductor,

00:29:14.310 --> 00:29:18.600
so the alpha is small
near the band gap.

00:29:18.600 --> 00:29:20.850
So it's not a good absorber.

00:29:20.850 --> 00:29:24.750
And because of that, you have
to use a pretty thick material

00:29:24.750 --> 00:29:28.780
to absorb the photons.

00:29:28.780 --> 00:29:36.010
And so that is a big problem
with the photovoltaics, silicon

00:29:36.010 --> 00:29:37.725
photovoltaic, the material cost.

00:29:44.730 --> 00:29:47.120
So any questions.

00:29:47.120 --> 00:29:49.920
So this is propagating
in the same medium.

00:29:49.920 --> 00:29:51.730
And the exponential law--

00:29:51.730 --> 00:29:53.340
so sometimes we can write--

00:29:53.340 --> 00:29:55.410
so this is the
Poynting vector, right?

00:29:55.410 --> 00:30:00.390
And it's the, say,
the power flux.

00:30:00.390 --> 00:30:05.160
And sometimes we
write intensity.

00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:09.540
Intensity is the energy
per unit solid angle.

00:30:09.540 --> 00:30:13.140
Intensity propagating
in a medium

00:30:13.140 --> 00:30:16.320
is exponential
alpha times x, where

00:30:16.320 --> 00:30:18.040
x is direction of propagation.

00:30:18.040 --> 00:30:21.600
This is another way to
write the same form.

00:30:21.600 --> 00:30:24.240
And this is also
called Beer's law.

00:30:29.520 --> 00:30:32.140
It's a consequence of
the Maxwell equation,

00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:34.300
but it's called the Beer's law.

00:30:36.820 --> 00:30:42.260
So if you have a light
comes in onto a surface.

00:30:42.260 --> 00:30:50.250
And what we wrote down here is
propagating inside the medium.

00:30:50.250 --> 00:30:54.200
So we have not talked about
how much is reflected.

00:30:54.200 --> 00:30:56.925
And what we talked
is, once you know

00:30:56.925 --> 00:31:01.340
this field in this direction,
at this point, the flux,

00:31:01.340 --> 00:31:05.370
and it will decay
exponentially inside.

00:31:05.370 --> 00:31:14.690
So a material could be very
flattened, but very absorbing.

00:31:14.690 --> 00:31:16.280
What does that mean?

00:31:16.280 --> 00:31:18.430
It's conflicting, right?

00:31:18.430 --> 00:31:24.040
So what does that mean is that
the reflectance is very large.

00:31:24.040 --> 00:31:28.450
The reflectance,
R, is very large.

00:31:28.450 --> 00:31:32.070
The material could
be 99% reflecting.

00:31:32.070 --> 00:31:36.970
But once the electromagnetic
wave gets into the material,

00:31:36.970 --> 00:31:40.700
the penetration
depth is very short.

00:31:40.700 --> 00:31:41.810
It's absorbed.

00:31:41.810 --> 00:31:45.590
Those that get into
the surface is absorbed

00:31:45.590 --> 00:31:46.770
in very short distance.

00:31:46.770 --> 00:31:50.080
In fact, all metals
behave that way.

00:31:50.080 --> 00:31:53.260
Metal is very reflective,
but the field--

00:31:53.260 --> 00:31:57.220
maybe 1% or 5% of this
wave gets into the metal,

00:31:57.220 --> 00:32:00.550
absorbed typically
in 10 nanometers,

00:32:00.550 --> 00:32:01.870
10 to 20 nanometers.

00:32:04.570 --> 00:32:08.470
But if you have
indirect-gap semiconductor,

00:32:08.470 --> 00:32:12.520
like silicon, this penetration
depth can be a millimeter.

00:32:12.520 --> 00:32:15.560
If you do millimeter, you
want to capture that material.

00:32:15.560 --> 00:32:17.425
So when you make a
solar cell, millimeter

00:32:17.425 --> 00:32:21.160
mean a lot more materials,
so this is expensive.

00:32:23.860 --> 00:32:30.070
So this is what's
inside propagation.

00:32:30.070 --> 00:32:33.340
And now let's turn
our attention to what

00:32:33.340 --> 00:32:37.510
happens at the interface, that
R. What's the reflectance?

00:32:37.510 --> 00:32:38.830
What's the transmittance?

00:32:42.990 --> 00:32:52.800
Reflection at one interface--

00:32:56.140 --> 00:33:00.850
and this is very
similar to the scalar

00:33:00.850 --> 00:33:03.100
wave from the
Schrodinger equation

00:33:03.100 --> 00:33:05.050
we talked the last lecture.

00:33:05.050 --> 00:33:12.580
And what we need is the field
on both sides of the interface

00:33:12.580 --> 00:33:14.410
and use the continuity relation.

00:33:14.410 --> 00:33:19.090
If you think about how we
did with the material wave ,

00:33:19.090 --> 00:33:20.770
the wave function here.

00:33:20.770 --> 00:33:23.560
You have the wave function
on the left equals right

00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:26.660
at interface, and derivative
equal to each other.

00:33:26.660 --> 00:33:30.070
So that's how we derive the
reflectance transmittance

00:33:30.070 --> 00:33:31.750
for material waves.

00:33:31.750 --> 00:33:36.250
And we do the same thing
for electromagnetic waves.

00:33:36.250 --> 00:33:46.210
So what I have here is
flat interface 1 and 2.

00:33:46.210 --> 00:33:54.070
And let me make my life slightly
easier by saying here is n1.

00:33:54.070 --> 00:33:57.910
I can write a capital N1.

00:33:57.910 --> 00:34:01.600
If I just write a small
N1, it means low loss.

00:34:01.600 --> 00:34:06.340
If I write a capital
N1, means it has loss.

00:34:06.340 --> 00:34:09.190
And here I can write a N2.

00:34:09.190 --> 00:34:13.060
And I'll extend to the
case when there's loss--

00:34:13.060 --> 00:34:14.170
discuss it.

00:34:14.170 --> 00:34:19.090
The mass is identical, but there
are some subtle differences.

00:34:19.090 --> 00:34:22.780
And I have the z direction.

00:34:22.780 --> 00:34:27.489
This is my z direction
wave propagation.

00:34:27.489 --> 00:34:32.719
And this is my x direction.

00:34:32.719 --> 00:34:36.110
And I have a wave comes
in towards the interface.

00:34:36.110 --> 00:34:39.679
This is my k direction.

00:34:39.679 --> 00:34:43.659
That's the incident
wave direction.

00:34:43.659 --> 00:34:47.170
And I have the
normal, the surface n.

00:34:50.960 --> 00:34:57.670
So ki here is angle
of incidence, theta i.

00:34:57.670 --> 00:35:04.090
And ki is the wave propagation
of the incident wave.

00:35:04.090 --> 00:35:09.180
Two vector-- two
lines form a plane.

00:35:09.180 --> 00:35:12.760
So this plane I call
is plane of incidence.

00:35:12.760 --> 00:35:16.710
This is how I define
my reference plane.

00:35:16.710 --> 00:35:18.690
So I have my plane of incidence.

00:35:30.090 --> 00:35:38.970
And this is formed by n and
ki these are the two vector

00:35:38.970 --> 00:35:42.540
for my plane of incidence.

00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:48.030
Now I have to say the
field is a vector field.

00:35:48.030 --> 00:35:51.420
It's perpendicular to ki.

00:35:51.420 --> 00:35:53.760
But I have to define
which direction,

00:35:53.760 --> 00:35:57.330
because it could be any of this
direction perpendicular to ki.

00:36:00.780 --> 00:36:05.190
But I can-- any of this vector
I can decompose into two,

00:36:05.190 --> 00:36:08.160
the sum of two vectors.

00:36:08.160 --> 00:36:11.670
So I can always define,
if one case is my--

00:36:11.670 --> 00:36:17.140
if I think this as my electric
field, is in the plane.

00:36:17.140 --> 00:36:20.980
The other case is
perpendicular to the plane.

00:36:20.980 --> 00:36:24.670
And once you know the solution,
is a linear combination

00:36:24.670 --> 00:36:27.150
of the two.

00:36:27.150 --> 00:36:29.660
So any other direction,
you decompose

00:36:29.660 --> 00:36:33.650
the in-plane and cross-plane
perpendicular direction.

00:36:37.200 --> 00:36:41.580
But then you have the choice
of, well, now depends on--

00:36:41.580 --> 00:36:45.790
if this is my electrical
field, my magnetic field--

00:36:45.790 --> 00:36:47.875
now, if you use the
right-hand rule,

00:36:47.875 --> 00:36:49.500
what's the direction
of magnetic field?

00:36:53.539 --> 00:36:54.706
AUDIENCE: It's going to be--

00:36:54.706 --> 00:36:55.610
AUDIENCE: Coming up.

00:36:55.610 --> 00:36:57.110
GANG CHEN: Coming up, right?

00:36:57.110 --> 00:37:02.990
So E incident-- and
that's a vector.

00:37:02.990 --> 00:37:06.600
And the magnetic
field is pointing up.

00:37:06.600 --> 00:37:07.560
OK.

00:37:07.560 --> 00:37:10.360
So there are three
names for this--

00:37:10.360 --> 00:37:11.740
depends on which one you--

00:37:11.740 --> 00:37:12.930
we need to remember.

00:37:12.930 --> 00:37:17.020
It turns out for over this many
years, I always get confused.

00:37:20.140 --> 00:37:24.880
I always say, OK, I like to
remember this as a TM wave.

00:37:24.880 --> 00:37:29.240
TM means Transverse Magnetic.

00:37:29.240 --> 00:37:34.160
So this case, what
I draw is TM wave.

00:37:34.160 --> 00:37:38.600
That's the magnetic field is
perpendicular to the plane

00:37:38.600 --> 00:37:40.900
of incidence.

00:37:40.900 --> 00:37:43.480
So three names--
the other two names

00:37:43.480 --> 00:37:46.430
is relative to the
electrical field, then.

00:37:46.430 --> 00:37:49.900
It's parallel to the
plane of the incidence.

00:37:49.900 --> 00:37:52.630
So here you either
call it the TM wave,

00:37:52.630 --> 00:37:54.970
or you call it the parallel--

00:37:54.970 --> 00:37:59.830
P wave-- or you use
the symbol of parallel.

00:37:59.830 --> 00:38:01.840
So it's three
different notations.

00:38:04.450 --> 00:38:09.000
What I have here is
for the electric field.

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:12.310
And here is-- when
I say transverse, is

00:38:12.310 --> 00:38:15.420
whatever what's follow.

00:38:15.420 --> 00:38:17.490
Transverse is a TM.

00:38:17.490 --> 00:38:19.830
That means magnetic
field is perpendicular.

00:38:19.830 --> 00:38:23.280
TE mean the electrical
field is perpendicular.

00:38:23.280 --> 00:38:27.240
So what I'm going to
derive is the situation

00:38:27.240 --> 00:38:31.650
where the magnetic field is
perpendicular to the plane

00:38:31.650 --> 00:38:32.910
of the incidence.

00:38:35.640 --> 00:38:38.520
And now I need to write--

00:38:38.520 --> 00:38:42.300
when the wave comes in,
I could have reflection.

00:38:42.300 --> 00:38:45.420
I have transmission.

00:38:45.420 --> 00:38:48.870
So here reflection,
the wave vector,

00:38:48.870 --> 00:38:51.225
and transmission,
the wave vector.

00:38:53.970 --> 00:38:57.530
And in each medium I
have a plane waveform,

00:38:57.530 --> 00:39:00.470
I know the plane waveform.

00:39:00.470 --> 00:39:02.120
This is my plane waveform.

00:39:02.120 --> 00:39:05.630
I do not know the amplitude.

00:39:05.630 --> 00:39:10.370
And my wave vector,
I need to relate

00:39:10.370 --> 00:39:14.960
to what direction the wave
is going for the reflected

00:39:14.960 --> 00:39:16.700
and transmitted.

00:39:16.700 --> 00:39:21.830
So here is my theta
R, if I use moment n,

00:39:21.830 --> 00:39:27.980
angle theta t to denote it.

00:39:27.980 --> 00:39:29.930
So I can write--

00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:34.505
because if I want to
write this k by the R--

00:39:34.505 --> 00:39:38.980
R is any point in the plane xyz.

00:39:38.980 --> 00:39:45.440
And k, I have to write it now
in terms of the notation I have.

00:39:45.440 --> 00:39:47.990
This k, I have to
say kx, ky, kz.

00:39:50.930 --> 00:39:56.000
And I write my k--

00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:59.340
univector, not a magnitude.

00:39:59.340 --> 00:40:01.625
This is the total.

00:40:01.625 --> 00:40:05.090
The total, of course,
is related to omega C.

00:40:05.090 --> 00:40:09.390
But what's the univector is
related to direction only.

00:40:09.390 --> 00:40:13.920
So the univector, I can write
it as this is the vector

00:40:13.920 --> 00:40:16.020
direction, so what's my--

00:40:16.020 --> 00:40:23.670
under my, say, z is k
times the cosine theta.

00:40:23.670 --> 00:40:24.660
Right?

00:40:24.660 --> 00:40:26.230
X is sine theta.

00:40:26.230 --> 00:40:34.130
So I have really my sine
theta i zero cosine theta i.

00:40:34.130 --> 00:40:38.570
And this is my
incident univector.

00:40:38.570 --> 00:40:50.000
And my univector of reflection
is here, R. So x direction

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:54.140
is still sine theta R0.

00:40:54.140 --> 00:40:56.780
But the z direction
is negative now.

00:40:56.780 --> 00:41:00.700
This is my
propagation direction.

00:41:00.700 --> 00:41:07.730
My z direction is negative--
so negative cosine theta R.

00:41:07.730 --> 00:41:10.880
And my t direction--

00:41:10.880 --> 00:41:20.000
oh, this is a univector is
sine theta t 0 cosine theta t.

00:41:20.000 --> 00:41:22.310
Now we encourage
you to-- everybody

00:41:22.310 --> 00:41:25.340
really get comfortable.

00:41:25.340 --> 00:41:27.870
It took me many, many
years to get comfortable.

00:41:27.870 --> 00:41:30.680
But at least you should
do your exercise.

00:41:30.680 --> 00:41:33.150
And let's say I'm
giving you TM wave.

00:41:33.150 --> 00:41:35.450
You can go back and
do TE wave and go

00:41:35.450 --> 00:41:38.330
through the derivation
of what's reflectance,

00:41:38.330 --> 00:41:41.750
what's transmittance when
we go through an interface.

00:41:41.750 --> 00:41:45.380
And I made a comment
in the last lecture.

00:41:45.380 --> 00:41:49.070
When people do electrical-- say
this material wave Maxwell--

00:41:49.070 --> 00:41:53.450
no, Schrodinger equation, we
did a lot more incidence, right?

00:41:53.450 --> 00:41:57.060
And here can see, I'm doing
general any angle of incidence.

00:41:57.060 --> 00:41:59.570
So you should go back
and redo that problem,

00:41:59.570 --> 00:42:00.540
any angle of incidence.

00:42:00.540 --> 00:42:01.580
You'll be able to do it.

00:42:04.650 --> 00:42:15.570
So now, what I do next is to
write a component because I

00:42:15.570 --> 00:42:19.200
need the boundary conditions.

00:42:19.200 --> 00:42:24.060
Recall, for the material
wave, Schrodinger equation

00:42:24.060 --> 00:42:26.250
is the wave function
is continuous.

00:42:26.250 --> 00:42:28.710
Derivative wave
function is continuous.

00:42:28.710 --> 00:42:31.950
And what's my corresponding
boundary condition

00:42:31.950 --> 00:42:34.770
for Maxwell equation?

00:42:34.770 --> 00:42:39.050
And it turns out
that any interface--

00:42:39.050 --> 00:42:40.880
and this is actually
very general.

00:42:40.880 --> 00:42:43.340
How you derive an
interface condition?

00:42:43.340 --> 00:42:45.440
When you do heat
transfer, you do the same.

00:42:45.440 --> 00:42:48.230
You apply-- so when
you do a heat transfer,

00:42:48.230 --> 00:42:50.450
you apply your boundary
condition to-- you

00:42:50.450 --> 00:42:52.610
apply your equation
of energy balance

00:42:52.610 --> 00:42:55.010
to both sides of the interface.

00:42:55.010 --> 00:42:56.960
So if I have-- this is a--

00:42:56.960 --> 00:42:59.960
let's say, many of you probably
more familiar with the heat

00:42:59.960 --> 00:43:03.770
transfer, so I'll try to
write down the boundary

00:43:03.770 --> 00:43:05.090
condition for this.

00:43:05.090 --> 00:43:08.630
If this is a liquid,
this is solid, right?

00:43:08.630 --> 00:43:10.670
Apply the energy conservation.

00:43:10.670 --> 00:43:13.190
I see on the solid side,
the heat conduction

00:43:13.190 --> 00:43:17.543
coming towards this interface
equals the convection going

00:43:17.543 --> 00:43:18.710
through the other interface.

00:43:18.710 --> 00:43:21.120
I'm applying the first law.

00:43:21.120 --> 00:43:23.550
The thickness is 0.

00:43:23.550 --> 00:43:25.200
There is heat
comes in from here,

00:43:25.200 --> 00:43:29.490
but my limit is thickness
0, so that term drops out.

00:43:29.490 --> 00:43:32.190
When you apply first rule,
you have four surfaces

00:43:32.190 --> 00:43:35.220
in my drawing here.

00:43:35.220 --> 00:43:39.150
So I do the same thing
when I do Maxwell equation.

00:43:39.150 --> 00:43:42.300
Or you do Schrodinger
equation-- how you derive--

00:43:42.300 --> 00:43:45.420
you apply, in the case
of Schrodinger equation,

00:43:45.420 --> 00:43:47.720
you have your
material wave that's

00:43:47.720 --> 00:43:50.370
saying the matter
must be continuous.

00:43:50.370 --> 00:43:54.270
With that you can write the
equation we gave before.

00:43:54.270 --> 00:43:57.270
And here, I have to apply--

00:43:57.270 --> 00:44:02.190
take that control volume,
apply all those four equations,

00:44:02.190 --> 00:44:05.270
integrate it over
that control volume

00:44:05.270 --> 00:44:09.125
and take the limit that
the thickness approaches 0.

00:44:11.760 --> 00:44:16.640
And with that you can write down
all your boundary conditions.

00:44:16.640 --> 00:44:22.520
And the boundary
condition is the n,

00:44:22.520 --> 00:44:33.500
the univector of the norm, and
D2 minus D1 equals rho surface.

00:44:33.500 --> 00:44:37.805
This is the real charge
accumulating on the surface.

00:44:41.570 --> 00:44:47.380
If you have a current flowing
uniformly through the material,

00:44:47.380 --> 00:44:50.410
everywhere you have
a current density.

00:44:50.410 --> 00:44:54.490
In that case, what's your
surface charge density?

00:44:54.490 --> 00:44:57.220
0 because everywhere is uniform.

00:44:57.220 --> 00:45:01.520
When you get your
thickness go to 0, that's

00:45:01.520 --> 00:45:04.320
the total number of
charge in this one,

00:45:04.320 --> 00:45:07.070
even a small thickness is 0.

00:45:07.070 --> 00:45:10.340
So normally this is 0.

00:45:10.340 --> 00:45:13.430
But if you do--

00:45:13.430 --> 00:45:19.610
let's say some of your may
work with electrochemistry.

00:45:19.610 --> 00:45:23.510
And in this case, you
have absorb the charge

00:45:23.510 --> 00:45:26.100
on the surface.

00:45:26.100 --> 00:45:28.740
And in that case, your
surface charge is not 0.

00:45:31.280 --> 00:45:35.260
So you can say what
is the n dot product.

00:45:35.260 --> 00:45:39.740
That means is the vertical
component, the component

00:45:39.740 --> 00:45:41.270
perpendicular to the interface.

00:45:41.270 --> 00:45:42.680
Because this is n direction.

00:45:42.680 --> 00:45:44.900
This is parallel to n direction.

00:45:44.900 --> 00:45:50.970
So basically, the displacement
field, the difference

00:45:50.970 --> 00:45:55.380
is the surface charge because
each surface charge add

00:45:55.380 --> 00:45:57.960
a coulomb field on top of it.

00:45:57.960 --> 00:46:02.040
The addition gives
you the difference

00:46:02.040 --> 00:46:06.770
in the displacement field.

00:46:06.770 --> 00:46:10.730
And then you have
the tangential then

00:46:10.730 --> 00:46:16.040
is a cross product
to the interface.

00:46:16.040 --> 00:46:19.910
So this is a parallel
component, is 0.

00:46:19.910 --> 00:46:22.580
So the electric
field is parallel

00:46:22.580 --> 00:46:24.080
to the interface and continuous.

00:46:28.250 --> 00:46:31.730
And then you do your magnetic.

00:46:31.730 --> 00:46:35.285
First is the dot
product, is zero.

00:46:39.980 --> 00:46:53.765
And the tangential component
is the surface charge--

00:46:56.410 --> 00:46:58.120
surface current.

00:46:58.120 --> 00:47:00.940
Again, the surface
current is something

00:47:00.940 --> 00:47:04.420
that you need to be careful.

00:47:04.420 --> 00:47:06.500
Really depends on, for example--

00:47:06.500 --> 00:47:07.510
I give you a case.

00:47:07.510 --> 00:47:11.860
If I have a graphene sheet,
I try to make a solar cell.

00:47:11.860 --> 00:47:16.090
And graphene sheet
is my electrode.

00:47:16.090 --> 00:47:19.750
And when I try to apply
the boundary condition,

00:47:19.750 --> 00:47:23.170
I will see that, in that case,
because of the graphene sheet

00:47:23.170 --> 00:47:25.450
has a much higher current
density than the rest

00:47:25.450 --> 00:47:31.070
of the region, I will take that
as my surface current density.

00:47:31.070 --> 00:47:34.330
But most of the time, if
this is homogeneous material

00:47:34.330 --> 00:47:37.910
and you take your infinite
thickness, this drops out.

00:47:37.910 --> 00:47:42.000
So what it also means
is the magnetic field,

00:47:42.000 --> 00:47:44.650
tangential component
is usually continuous.

00:47:44.650 --> 00:47:49.006
So basically, electrical field
is continuous because D--

00:47:49.006 --> 00:47:52.830
no, this D has to
be epsilon 2 D2--

00:47:52.830 --> 00:47:55.830
E2 epsilon 1 E1.

00:47:55.830 --> 00:47:59.640
But tangential component is
continuous electrical field.

00:47:59.640 --> 00:48:04.440
And magnetic field, the
perpendicular component

00:48:04.440 --> 00:48:07.530
is continuous, and the
tangential component

00:48:07.530 --> 00:48:11.880
is the difference of
the electrical current,

00:48:11.880 --> 00:48:14.062
surface current.

00:48:14.062 --> 00:48:15.520
The other with the
singular surface

00:48:15.520 --> 00:48:20.200
current is, you know that on
a wire through a conductor

00:48:20.200 --> 00:48:23.350
current, you've got a magnetic
field that's surrounding.

00:48:23.350 --> 00:48:24.950
Right?

00:48:24.950 --> 00:48:30.560
So when I have a surface
current flowing here,

00:48:30.560 --> 00:48:37.610
I have a magnetic field going
in the tangential direction.

00:48:37.610 --> 00:48:39.820
That's why you have
this relationship.

00:48:39.820 --> 00:48:44.470
But that's all derived from
applying the Maxwell equation

00:48:44.470 --> 00:48:47.990
to the interface.

00:48:47.990 --> 00:48:50.340
So those are the
general conditions.

00:48:50.340 --> 00:48:54.140
And now I'm going to
apply those conditions.

00:48:54.140 --> 00:48:55.880
I need to write down.

00:48:55.880 --> 00:48:58.880
I do a little bit dirty work--

00:48:58.880 --> 00:49:02.690
write down all those
components, tangential

00:49:02.690 --> 00:49:06.830
and perpendicular components,
and apply the boundary

00:49:06.830 --> 00:49:07.490
conditions.

00:49:11.110 --> 00:49:15.030
Need to write electrical
field, magnetic field.

00:49:25.290 --> 00:49:33.230
So-- but you need
to develop a habit.

00:49:33.230 --> 00:49:34.610
Yeah, it's all plane wave.

00:49:34.610 --> 00:49:36.980
That's what I wrote down before.

00:49:36.980 --> 00:49:42.620
And for the TM wave, where
the electric field is what I--

00:49:42.620 --> 00:49:44.030
incident, right?

00:49:44.030 --> 00:49:45.755
So it's an incident.

00:49:49.070 --> 00:49:50.780
I have three waves.

00:49:50.780 --> 00:49:52.745
One is the incident,
the other is reflective,

00:49:52.745 --> 00:49:54.020
the other is transmitted.

00:49:54.020 --> 00:49:57.770
I have to write down
all of them to count.

00:49:57.770 --> 00:50:00.710
So this is the incident,
and it's a vector

00:50:00.710 --> 00:50:05.665
because it's not parallel to x
or parallel to any direction.

00:50:05.665 --> 00:50:08.240
It has an angle.

00:50:08.240 --> 00:50:13.950
And then exponential, I need
to carry my phase factor,

00:50:13.950 --> 00:50:20.340
minus i omega t minus--

00:50:20.340 --> 00:50:24.270
you go to look at what
we have here-- k dot r.

00:50:24.270 --> 00:50:31.740
k I already pull out, so omega
C0 times N. And now I have ki

00:50:31.740 --> 00:50:34.590
is sine theta i cosine theta i0.

00:50:37.690 --> 00:50:39.490
And r is xyz.

00:50:39.490 --> 00:50:51.390
So the top product of these
two gives me N1x Xi sine theta

00:50:51.390 --> 00:50:59.400
i plus N1z cosine theta i.

00:50:59.400 --> 00:51:03.020
So this is where we
should be careful--

00:51:03.020 --> 00:51:03.800
and C0.

00:51:07.737 --> 00:51:08.570
That's the incident.

00:51:12.020 --> 00:51:17.190
And it's really tedious,
but once you get used to it,

00:51:17.190 --> 00:51:20.580
this is just a phase factor.

00:51:20.580 --> 00:51:25.860
And remember, this one
actually has a component

00:51:25.860 --> 00:51:30.420
because the vector Ei has
a component in x direction,

00:51:30.420 --> 00:51:34.770
