That's a [INAUDIBLE].

00:55:51.210 --> 00:55:54.530
It's when you substitute it into
the equation, you'll get this.

00:55:54.530 --> 00:56:02.930
So mu zero C0 and
exponential t--

00:56:02.930 --> 00:56:06.590
let me write this phase
factor is the same.

00:56:06.590 --> 00:56:11.330
Phase factor is the
same as reflected,

00:56:11.330 --> 00:56:21.680
and n2 mu 0 C0 and parallel--
oh, this is r, reflected.

00:56:21.680 --> 00:56:23.600
This is a transmitted--

00:56:23.600 --> 00:56:26.720
exponential phase
factor of transmitting.

00:56:26.720 --> 00:56:30.800
So here, what [INAUDIBLE]
in this one is phi incident,

00:56:30.800 --> 00:56:33.890
and this is the phi reflected.

00:56:33.890 --> 00:56:37.760
And what's inside here
is my phi transmitted.

00:56:41.800 --> 00:56:45.280
So what really is
tedious is carrying out

00:56:45.280 --> 00:56:48.160
this phase factor, which
will drop out very quickly.

00:56:50.900 --> 00:56:54.920
Now I'm going to
apply the continuity

00:56:54.920 --> 00:57:00.410
The electric field
tangential component,

00:57:00.410 --> 00:57:02.607
because I don't have
any surface charge--

00:57:02.607 --> 00:57:04.940
tangential component, electric
field, and magnetic field

00:57:04.940 --> 00:57:08.520
are all continuous.

00:57:08.520 --> 00:57:11.190
And you see, you could
apply the perpendicular

00:57:11.190 --> 00:57:13.350
field is continuous.

00:57:13.350 --> 00:57:18.030
And either way, you'll
get the same result.

00:57:18.030 --> 00:57:23.310
So let me apply this relation.

00:57:23.310 --> 00:57:30.740
What I have here is the
tangential component, so

00:57:30.740 --> 00:57:31.505
electric field.

00:57:40.270 --> 00:57:45.400
And my electric field is in
the tangential component,

00:57:45.400 --> 00:57:50.050
is Ex, continuous
in the x direction.

00:57:50.050 --> 00:57:54.610
If you look at it,
my electric field

00:57:54.610 --> 00:57:59.260
in the x direction for
incident, for reflected--

00:57:59.260 --> 00:58:02.580
I have to project it
into all x direction.

00:58:02.580 --> 00:58:04.050
And that's so the field--

00:58:04.050 --> 00:58:06.720
you need to sum up each side.

00:58:06.720 --> 00:58:07.750
It's a total field.

00:58:07.750 --> 00:58:09.030
It's not just one.

00:58:09.030 --> 00:58:11.040
I didn't say incident
or reflected.

00:58:11.040 --> 00:58:13.620
It's the total
field on each side.

00:58:13.620 --> 00:58:15.360
Same when we do
the wave function.

00:58:15.360 --> 00:58:19.370
It's the total wave function
due to incident and reflection.

00:58:19.370 --> 00:58:24.410
So this field summation is
very different than when

00:58:24.410 --> 00:58:25.610
you do this--

00:58:25.610 --> 00:58:27.980
typically, if you've
taken radiation,

00:58:27.980 --> 00:58:29.900
it's doing intensity add up.

00:58:29.900 --> 00:58:32.570
Now I'm doing in
the field add up.

00:58:32.570 --> 00:58:34.240
And that equals the other side.

00:58:34.240 --> 00:58:42.530
So if I do this, what
I have here is Eix,

00:58:42.530 --> 00:58:45.140
so incident x component.

00:58:45.140 --> 00:58:50.030
And exponential, I need to
carry this phase factor.

00:58:50.030 --> 00:58:52.790
Z is 0.

00:58:52.790 --> 00:58:55.280
I was clever choosing
my coordinate.

00:58:55.280 --> 00:58:58.950
Z is 0 at the interface.

00:58:58.950 --> 00:59:02.530
So all z's drop out.

00:59:02.530 --> 00:59:03.820
Right?

00:59:03.820 --> 00:59:06.880
And omega t, i omega
t, you look at it.

00:59:06.880 --> 00:59:09.040
Every term has a
negative i omega t.

00:59:09.040 --> 00:59:11.710
That will drop off.

00:59:11.710 --> 00:59:13.190
Right?

00:59:13.190 --> 00:59:17.060
So I'm not going to carry
[INAUDIBLE] i omega t.

00:59:17.060 --> 00:59:18.550
I'm not writing down z.

00:59:18.550 --> 00:59:20.090
Z equal 0.

00:59:20.090 --> 00:59:22.770
And I'm only x.

00:59:22.770 --> 00:59:27.120
So I'm going to write
this x component term--

00:59:27.120 --> 00:59:38.070
is i omega n1x and
sine theta i over C0.

00:59:38.070 --> 00:59:43.020
That's the incident
component in the x direction.

00:59:43.020 --> 00:59:50.310
And the reflected component in
the x direction, exponential i

00:59:50.310 --> 00:59:52.150
omega.

00:59:52.150 --> 01:00:00.870
n1x sine theta r
equals- over C0--

01:00:00.870 --> 01:00:09.360
equals transmitted in the x
direction exponential i omega.

01:00:09.360 --> 01:00:17.250
n2x sine theta i over C0.

01:00:17.250 --> 01:00:21.750
So this is the continuity
in the electrical field

01:00:21.750 --> 01:00:25.320
in the x direction.

01:00:25.320 --> 01:00:30.560
I can ride the magnetic
field similarly.

01:00:30.560 --> 01:00:33.890
But I want to do one argument
so that I can drop out

01:00:33.890 --> 01:00:34.880
all those exponents.

01:00:37.400 --> 01:00:39.090
You can look at this.

01:00:39.090 --> 01:00:42.740
This equation has to
be valid for x point,

01:00:42.740 --> 01:00:48.440
every point x in the plane.

01:00:48.440 --> 01:00:51.740
For that to happen,
your only way

01:00:51.740 --> 01:00:55.170
is all that exponential
equal to each other.

01:00:55.170 --> 01:00:58.440
Otherwise, you
have zero solution.

01:00:58.440 --> 01:00:59.320
Right?

01:00:59.320 --> 01:01:02.380
Because I only have one
transmitted one reflected.

01:01:02.380 --> 01:01:10.120
So x-- for this equation to
have a long term solution,

01:01:10.120 --> 01:01:15.210
all exponential terms
equal to each other.

01:01:15.210 --> 01:01:19.650
And when I have this omega,
of course, doesn't change.

01:01:19.650 --> 01:01:25.310
And so you can see,
the n1 sine theta i,

01:01:25.310 --> 01:01:34.147
from here equal n1 sine theta
r equals n2 sine theta t.

01:01:37.069 --> 01:01:45.190
If that happens, it gives me
all the exponent are equal.

01:01:45.190 --> 01:01:48.330
So this is what you learned
in high school, right?

01:01:48.330 --> 01:01:54.240
Optics-- the incident angle
equals reflected angle--

01:01:54.240 --> 01:01:57.480
Snell Law, right?

01:01:57.480 --> 01:02:01.530
This solution is theta
i equals theta r.

01:02:01.530 --> 01:02:04.680
And n1 sine theta i
equals n2 sine theta t.

01:02:04.680 --> 01:02:07.360
That's a refractional.

01:02:07.360 --> 01:02:09.530
Right?

01:02:09.530 --> 01:02:15.410
So this gives me theta
i equals theta r.

01:02:15.410 --> 01:02:22.400
And n1 sine theta i
equals n2 sine theta t.

01:02:25.790 --> 01:02:28.410
So this is a Snell law.

01:02:28.410 --> 01:02:31.690
And another way to
think about this

01:02:31.690 --> 01:02:38.360
is, if you look back into
our general solution,

01:02:38.360 --> 01:02:41.860
this exponent is kx--

01:02:41.860 --> 01:02:44.500
kx times x.

01:02:44.500 --> 01:02:51.710
So what I have here,
is a kx times x.

01:02:51.710 --> 01:02:55.640
So kx is the continuous.

01:02:55.640 --> 01:03:02.060
So kx must be, say, i
incident equals kx reflected

01:03:02.060 --> 01:03:07.640
equals kx transmitted.

01:03:07.640 --> 01:03:13.030
And this is an often called the
lateral momentum conservation.

01:03:13.030 --> 01:03:16.570
The momentum component
in the direction parallel

01:03:16.570 --> 01:03:20.960
to the interface are
conserved for incident,

01:03:20.960 --> 01:03:25.130
reflected, and transmitted.

01:03:25.130 --> 01:03:31.100
So it turns out, depends
on who you're talking to,

01:03:31.100 --> 01:03:32.930
people use a completely
different term.

01:03:36.680 --> 01:03:39.410
Of course, for a specular
smooth surface-- here

01:03:39.410 --> 01:03:40.650
we say very smooth.

01:03:40.650 --> 01:03:41.930
We don't have many--

01:03:41.930 --> 01:03:44.840
any assumption of
surface roughness.

01:03:44.840 --> 01:03:48.475
In this case, I have an incident
equal reflection and Snell

01:03:48.475 --> 01:03:50.550
law valid.

01:03:50.550 --> 01:03:53.040
And then, say--

01:03:53.040 --> 01:03:59.670
I think you heard me talk about
the gratings, Bragg reflection,

01:03:59.670 --> 01:04:00.210
right?

01:04:00.210 --> 01:04:05.700
If I have periodic
structure on the surface,

01:04:05.700 --> 01:04:08.850
and it turns out this is
momentum conservation--

01:04:08.850 --> 01:04:14.400
this momentum is like crystal
momentum is not exactly--

01:04:14.400 --> 01:04:16.300
you have to always obey it.

01:04:16.300 --> 01:04:20.100
So the structure, when it has
a component in the x direction,

01:04:20.100 --> 01:04:23.710
in this case if it's a periodic
structure in the x direction,

01:04:23.710 --> 01:04:28.230
it gives you the structure,
the geometrical component

01:04:28.230 --> 01:04:30.010
of wave vector in
this direction.

01:04:30.010 --> 01:04:33.130
That's the Bragg condition.

01:04:33.130 --> 01:04:37.570
So when you have a light comes
in, say periodic structure,

01:04:37.570 --> 01:04:43.240
you have reflection
only in certain spots.

01:04:43.240 --> 01:04:45.710
In this case is the
crystal providing

01:04:45.710 --> 01:04:47.980
your lateral momentum.

01:04:47.980 --> 01:04:52.600
So this momentum
conservation rule here,

01:04:52.600 --> 01:04:58.200
lateral momentum conservation,
if you have roughness,

01:04:58.200 --> 01:05:00.690
actually your light
can go many directions.

01:05:00.690 --> 01:05:03.150
So if you complete
a rough random,

01:05:03.150 --> 01:05:07.170
your reflection actually can
go, in the case of periodic,

01:05:07.170 --> 01:05:08.670
it goes certain spots.

01:05:08.670 --> 01:05:13.720
And if it's rough, it
goes all directions.

01:05:13.720 --> 01:05:17.680
So it's here is a roughened
surface that provides you

01:05:17.680 --> 01:05:21.940
this geometrical momentum
needed to obey the momentum

01:05:21.940 --> 01:05:23.950
conservation rule.

01:05:23.950 --> 01:05:26.590
So like I said, depends
on who you talk to.

01:05:26.590 --> 01:05:29.680
And then when I deal with
the lateral magnetic wave,

01:05:29.680 --> 01:05:32.860
people normally say
this is a rough surface

01:05:32.860 --> 01:05:34.780
and diffused reflection.

01:05:34.780 --> 01:05:37.510
You talk to electrical
engineer, you

01:05:37.510 --> 01:05:39.100
check the electrical
literature, they

01:05:39.100 --> 01:05:40.720
don't talk about rough surface.

01:05:40.720 --> 01:05:43.300
They always say, OK, it's a
momentum conservative, long

01:05:43.300 --> 01:05:45.370
conserve.

01:05:45.370 --> 01:05:46.630
It's talking about same thing.

01:05:51.690 --> 01:05:55.480
So now with that, I drop
off all the exponents.

01:05:55.480 --> 01:05:58.380
You can see here, this
equals this, equals this.

01:05:58.380 --> 01:06:03.940
So I have written a lot
of complex expressions.

01:06:03.940 --> 01:06:09.950
Now I'm going to simplify this.

01:06:09.950 --> 01:06:11.270
Let me write here.

01:06:18.750 --> 01:06:30.990
And I'm going to simplify to
have Eix plus Eir equals Etx.

01:06:30.990 --> 01:06:33.210
That's my-- this gives--

01:06:33.210 --> 01:06:39.060
the Snell law gives me the x
component of the electric field

01:06:39.060 --> 01:06:40.530
is continuous--

01:06:40.530 --> 01:06:41.760
the magnitude now.

01:06:41.760 --> 01:06:44.420
The phase factor already taken
care of by the Snell law.

01:06:47.180 --> 01:06:56.820
And of course, the Eix
is the Ei cosine theta i.

01:06:56.820 --> 01:06:59.970
And this is a
parallel component.

01:06:59.970 --> 01:07:02.480
This is where I keep
talking about the TM wave--

01:07:02.480 --> 01:07:11.750
plus E parallel r reflected
cosine theta r equals

01:07:11.750 --> 01:07:15.870
E transmitted cosine theta t.

01:07:15.870 --> 01:07:25.750
So this is written in terms of
the amplitude of the incident,

01:07:25.750 --> 01:07:28.630
reflected, transmitted field.

01:07:28.630 --> 01:07:31.540
Now I have my next relation.

01:07:31.540 --> 01:07:33.250
This is the magnetic field.

01:07:33.250 --> 01:07:36.260
This is continuous.

01:07:36.260 --> 01:07:40.360
Magnetic field is the y
direction and doesn't have--

01:07:40.360 --> 01:07:42.820
because it's only y direction.

01:07:42.820 --> 01:07:46.070
You see, this is
all y component.

01:07:46.070 --> 01:07:53.140
So on the first media, I
have the sum of these two.

01:07:53.140 --> 01:07:54.520
The phase factor is the same--

01:07:54.520 --> 01:07:58.910
Snell law-- equals
the second medium.

01:07:58.910 --> 01:08:03.120
So what I have here is n1.

01:08:03.120 --> 01:08:06.590
And in fact, the
mu C cancel, right?

01:08:06.590 --> 01:08:07.810
Mu C is the same.

01:08:07.810 --> 01:08:15.670
So n1 E parallel i minus
here the reflected--

01:08:15.670 --> 01:08:26.140
is n1 E parallel r equals
n2 on the other side--

01:08:26.140 --> 01:08:28.810
E parallel t.

01:08:28.810 --> 01:08:35.359
So those are the two
equations I went through to--

01:08:35.359 --> 01:08:37.479
I'm looking for.

01:08:37.479 --> 01:08:41.260
I'm looking for how
much is reflected

01:08:41.260 --> 01:08:44.200
versus the incident,
how much is transmitted

01:08:44.200 --> 01:08:47.080
field versus the incident.

01:08:47.080 --> 01:08:48.990
And I have enough
equation to do that.

01:08:51.870 --> 01:08:56.040
So now you go to
solve for this ratio.

01:08:56.040 --> 01:09:00.840
And I have my
reflection coefficient

01:09:00.840 --> 01:09:13.109
is E parallel r E parallel
i equals n1 cosine thetas

01:09:13.109 --> 01:09:23.100
t minus n2 cosine theta
i And n1 cosine theta

01:09:23.100 --> 01:09:27.359
t plus n2 cosine theta i.

01:09:27.359 --> 01:09:31.770
So this is the
reflection coefficient.

01:09:31.770 --> 01:09:37.620
And transmission coefficient
is a 2n1 cosine theta

01:09:37.620 --> 01:09:45.600
i and n1 cosine theta i--

01:09:45.600 --> 01:09:50.010
no, theta t plus
n2 cosine theta i--

01:09:50.010 --> 01:09:51.939
same denominator.

01:09:51.939 --> 01:09:56.790
So those are the reflection
and transmission coefficient.

01:09:56.790 --> 01:09:59.490
It's not a reflectance
or transmittance yet.

01:10:04.701 --> 01:10:06.770
AUDIENCE: In the first
term on the far right,

01:10:06.770 --> 01:10:08.730
n2 cosine theta
i, is that right?

01:10:08.730 --> 01:10:09.230
So you're--

01:10:09.230 --> 01:10:09.938
GANG CHEN: Right.

01:10:09.938 --> 01:10:11.703
And so you cross this.

01:10:11.703 --> 01:10:12.620
AUDIENCE: It's not n1?

01:10:12.620 --> 01:10:16.780
GANG CHEN: This is a n1 cosine
theta t, n2 cosine theta i.

01:10:16.780 --> 01:10:18.050
OK?

01:10:18.050 --> 01:10:19.392
They switch.

01:10:19.392 --> 01:10:20.810
AUDIENCE: N2 cosine theta i.

01:10:20.810 --> 01:10:21.770
GANG CHEN: Right.

01:10:21.770 --> 01:10:23.240
Yeah.

01:10:23.240 --> 01:10:26.330
It's different expression
if you look at the t.

01:10:26.330 --> 01:10:28.940
So if you look at--

01:10:28.940 --> 01:10:31.040
if it's tE
polarization, you'll get

01:10:31.040 --> 01:10:32.300
a slight different expression.

01:10:32.300 --> 01:10:33.990
But it's a similar.

01:10:33.990 --> 01:10:35.240
So I would not remember this.

01:10:35.240 --> 01:10:36.500
Every time I have to check.

01:10:40.570 --> 01:10:44.650
But what we have
now is the magnitude

01:10:44.650 --> 01:10:51.040
of reflected and
transmitted fields.

01:10:51.040 --> 01:10:54.340
And based on this,
I can go further,

01:10:54.340 --> 01:10:57.880
calculate the Poynting vector.

01:10:57.880 --> 01:11:06.490
I will calculate
my Poynting vector

01:11:06.490 --> 01:11:08.035
because I want to
find the energy.

01:11:12.150 --> 01:11:15.330
So your Poynting vector--

01:11:15.330 --> 01:11:17.730
and you can say,
for this case, you

01:11:17.730 --> 01:11:21.600
have a component
in the x direction.

01:11:21.600 --> 01:11:24.000
You have component
in the z direction.

01:11:27.750 --> 01:11:31.410
And what you really care when
you go through a interface,

01:11:31.410 --> 01:11:33.160
at least if you
look at transport

01:11:33.160 --> 01:11:35.400
in the interface
direction is what's

01:11:35.400 --> 01:11:38.640
the component in
the z direction.

01:11:38.640 --> 01:11:44.300
That's the energy flux
going across the interface.

01:11:44.300 --> 01:11:48.440
So if you check your
Poynting vector,

01:11:48.440 --> 01:11:58.430
and we will define
reflectance, R

01:11:58.430 --> 01:12:03.620
equals parallel
in the z direction

01:12:03.620 --> 01:12:06.980
reflected incident
in the z direction.

01:12:06.980 --> 01:12:10.220
And you see, it's just the
reflection coefficient squared.

01:12:14.220 --> 01:12:18.180
And that's because, if you go
to check your load, Poynting

01:12:18.180 --> 01:12:22.980
vector S, in the
homogeneous media,

01:12:22.980 --> 01:12:28.080
you would say there is something
like a complex reflective

01:12:28.080 --> 01:12:30.310
index.

01:12:30.310 --> 01:12:34.480
But because it's in the
same media, that cancels.

01:12:34.480 --> 01:12:39.205
So that's just a few pages
ago we talked about it

01:12:39.205 --> 01:12:41.180
at the beginning, right?

01:12:41.180 --> 01:12:48.690
And the transmittance--
in fact, maybe I

01:12:48.690 --> 01:12:53.760
should have used transmisivity
for a flat surface.

01:12:53.760 --> 01:12:57.810
As I said, if you
do reverse, it's

01:12:57.810 --> 01:13:01.050
an intrinsic material property.

01:13:01.050 --> 01:13:04.440
But if you have rough, we do
reflectance transmittance.

01:13:04.440 --> 01:13:08.070
If it's a intrinsic, it's
reflectivity transmisivity.

01:13:08.070 --> 01:13:09.935
And here is the idea.

01:13:09.935 --> 01:13:13.860
And so that's if you have ideal
surface, you always have this.

01:13:13.860 --> 01:13:22.240
So transmittance,
tau-- it doesn't

01:13:22.240 --> 01:13:25.930
matter whether it's a parallel
or perpendicular wave.

01:13:25.930 --> 01:13:28.840
But here, what I have
is for transmittance

01:13:28.840 --> 01:13:32.650
I have to be careful because
the Poynting vector is going

01:13:32.650 --> 01:13:34.520
from one side to the other.

01:13:34.520 --> 01:13:44.920
So I have N2 cosine theta
t and the real part of N1.

01:13:44.920 --> 01:13:49.180
So this is when the theta i--

01:13:49.180 --> 01:13:58.810
this is when both sides have a,
say, complex reflective index.

01:13:58.810 --> 01:14:04.225
This here is where it's a
little bit more complex.

01:14:07.250 --> 01:14:10.970
So here is called a
Fresnel Coefficient--

01:14:13.665 --> 01:14:14.165
French.

01:14:22.530 --> 01:14:25.800
So Fresnel Coefficients,
for reflection transmission

01:14:25.800 --> 01:14:31.380
at the interface, here is
for parallel polarized.

01:14:31.380 --> 01:14:32.910
So that's the electric field.

01:14:32.910 --> 01:14:34.770
That is in the
plane of incidence.

01:14:34.770 --> 01:14:39.730
And let me put a parallel here.

01:14:39.730 --> 01:14:43.440
And if it's a electric
field in the perpendicular

01:14:43.440 --> 01:14:46.500
plane of incidence, you go
through the same derivation.

01:14:46.500 --> 01:14:49.890
And there are different set
of Fresnel Coefficients.

01:14:49.890 --> 01:14:56.220
And here it gives you the
reflectance and transmittance

01:14:56.220 --> 01:14:58.050
based on those coefficients.

01:15:01.520 --> 01:15:07.020
So let me make a
few more comments.

01:15:07.020 --> 01:15:10.710
Here are we see this is a--

01:15:10.710 --> 01:15:13.890
we discussed the name here.

01:15:13.890 --> 01:15:15.480
This is a TM.

01:15:15.480 --> 01:15:18.570
The other name is--

01:15:18.570 --> 01:15:20.500
so here is a TM wave.

01:15:20.500 --> 01:15:24.270
If the electrical field is
perpendicular to the plane

01:15:24.270 --> 01:15:26.370
the incidence, it's
called a T wave.

01:15:26.370 --> 01:15:31.710
And this is a S and
perpendicular sign.

01:15:31.710 --> 01:15:34.200
So it depends on
which book you read,

01:15:34.200 --> 01:15:37.240
you use it's own notation.

01:15:37.240 --> 01:15:40.780
And in fact, there is
even more confusion

01:15:40.780 --> 01:15:43.150
if you read a different book.

01:15:43.150 --> 01:15:46.930
And sometimes the people are
write N equals n minus i kappa.

01:15:50.300 --> 01:15:53.120
I wrote a n plus i kappa.

01:15:53.120 --> 01:15:57.950
And that depends on whether, in
this waveform factor plane wave

01:15:57.950 --> 01:16:04.150
expression, whether you put
a negative sign in the front.

01:16:04.150 --> 01:16:07.350
If you don't use
this selective sign,

01:16:07.350 --> 01:16:10.920
you should have a
n minus i kappa.

01:16:10.920 --> 01:16:12.810
So I like to put
the negative sign

01:16:12.810 --> 01:16:15.870
so that it's a n plus i kappa.

01:16:15.870 --> 01:16:19.120
Different books use
different notation.

01:16:19.120 --> 01:16:20.875
And there is no consistency.

01:16:20.875 --> 01:16:22.000
I can't solve that problem.

01:16:24.820 --> 01:16:28.960
The other is let's look
at this expression.

01:16:28.960 --> 01:16:32.150
And in fact, you read
a [INAUDIBLE] paper,

01:16:32.150 --> 01:16:35.110
if you have are
doing your homework.

01:16:35.110 --> 01:16:41.060
He used exactly what we
have here, Snell law,

01:16:41.060 --> 01:16:46.850
for surface wave, for when
the epsilon mu is negative.

01:16:46.850 --> 01:16:49.630
And sometimes this
goes to infinite.

01:16:49.630 --> 01:16:52.620
This r itself goes to infinite.

01:16:52.620 --> 01:16:54.660
What that mean the
r goes to infinite?

01:16:54.660 --> 01:16:57.560
It just means that there's no
wave can come in and couple

01:16:57.560 --> 01:16:58.630
to the surface.

01:16:58.630 --> 01:17:04.200
So in that case, what it
has is a surface wave.

01:17:04.200 --> 01:17:08.280
And the wave decays
exponentially

01:17:08.280 --> 01:17:09.900
from both sides of the surface.

01:17:17.710 --> 01:17:24.190
So what it have is a wave
that decays exponentially

01:17:24.190 --> 01:17:28.040
from the surface, both sides.

01:17:28.040 --> 01:17:31.780
And this is where he was
discussing different solutions

01:17:31.780 --> 01:17:33.620
of the Maxwell equation.

01:17:33.620 --> 01:17:36.130
So hopefully you
see that it's not

01:17:36.130 --> 01:17:38.200
too far from what we discussed.

01:17:38.200 --> 01:17:41.410
You just need to recognize this.

01:17:41.410 --> 01:17:46.098
And also, when theta i is 0--

01:17:46.098 --> 01:17:47.140
that's a normal incident.

01:17:49.660 --> 01:17:53.590
When theta i is 0, cosine
theta t, all this are 0,

01:17:53.590 --> 01:18:02.140
so what I have here is r
equals n1 minus n2 n1 plus n2.

01:18:06.270 --> 01:18:12.460
So if you go to check
for the material

01:18:12.460 --> 01:18:15.350
wave we derived at
the last lecture,

01:18:15.350 --> 01:18:19.000
it's k1 minus k2, k1 plus k2.

01:18:19.000 --> 01:18:20.530
It's the same expression.

01:18:20.530 --> 01:18:23.890
And in fact, you
can write into k--

01:18:23.890 --> 01:18:26.460
[INAUDIBLE] use k completely--

01:18:26.460 --> 01:18:27.210
[INAUDIBLE] paper.

01:18:27.210 --> 01:18:28.430
You go to read, he used k.

01:18:28.430 --> 01:18:32.040
He didn't use n, so that
he can have epsilon.

01:18:32.040 --> 01:18:35.880
He did not use n
because, whether you

01:18:35.880 --> 01:18:38.280
take a positive root,
a negative root--

01:18:38.280 --> 01:18:42.390
that's for the debate there.

01:18:42.390 --> 01:18:46.770
But in this case, R is--

01:18:46.770 --> 01:18:51.450
the reflectance R--
is the R squared,

01:18:51.450 --> 01:18:54.710
so giving you an
order of magnitude.

01:18:54.710 --> 01:18:56.280
So you can see
it's very similar.

01:18:56.280 --> 01:18:58.200
The wave expressing
all very similar--

01:18:58.200 --> 01:19:01.740
reflectance, transmittance.

01:19:01.740 --> 01:19:04.800
But let's say glass.

01:19:04.800 --> 01:19:10.510
Glass n is about 1.5.

01:19:10.510 --> 01:19:14.860
How much reflection is
interface of glass has.

01:19:14.860 --> 01:19:21.900
Air is 1, so 1.5 minus
1.5, divide by 2.5.

01:19:21.900 --> 01:19:24.260
That's one phase.

01:19:24.260 --> 01:19:30.050
Square-- 1/25 1/25 is what?

01:19:30.050 --> 01:19:31.860
4%?

01:19:31.860 --> 01:19:32.670
Right?

01:19:32.670 --> 01:19:36.780
So typically, one glass
interface give you 4%,

01:19:36.780 --> 01:19:39.810
and a glass has to interface.

01:19:39.810 --> 01:19:43.190
So that's 0.96 line times 0.96.

01:19:43.190 --> 01:19:46.410
So glass transmittance
is about 92%, 93%.

01:19:49.200 --> 01:19:53.785
It looks like fine, unless you
really care about efficiency.

01:19:53.785 --> 01:19:57.090
And 92%, if you put a
[INAUDIBLE] glass there--

01:19:57.090 --> 01:20:00.360
layer there-- in
solar cells, and then

01:20:00.360 --> 01:20:04.800
gaps, and you'll get
a, say, below the 90%.

01:20:04.800 --> 01:20:06.900
You'll get the loss
of 10% of your energy.

01:20:06.900 --> 01:20:08.460
That's a lot.

01:20:08.460 --> 01:20:11.580
Sometimes it looks small.

01:20:11.580 --> 01:20:14.870
Secondly, if you
look at the silicon--

01:20:14.870 --> 01:20:17.630
so it's good to
remember these numbers.

01:20:17.630 --> 01:20:23.190
Silicon-- anything about 3.5.

01:20:23.190 --> 01:20:27.210
So 3.5 minus 1-- so
silicon interface,

01:20:27.210 --> 01:20:28.230
how much reflection is?

01:20:28.230 --> 01:20:32.710
2.5 divided by 4.5 square.

01:20:32.710 --> 01:20:33.490
Right?

01:20:33.490 --> 01:20:38.980
2.5 divided by 4.5,
that's about 50%.

01:20:38.980 --> 01:20:43.180
50% square, 25%, right?

01:20:43.180 --> 01:20:50.870
So the glass of interface
reflection is about 25%, 30%.

01:20:50.870 --> 01:20:52.370
If you heat silicon--

01:20:52.370 --> 01:20:54.890
if all the light is absorbed--

01:20:54.890 --> 01:20:58.670
of course, in between the
gap, you don't get absorbed--

01:20:58.670 --> 01:21:00.680
then the emittance
of silicon then

01:21:00.680 --> 01:21:05.650
is about 0.7 because
the reflection is 30%,

01:21:05.650 --> 01:21:07.870
and the rest of
it gets absorbed.

01:21:07.870 --> 01:21:13.090
Absorption equals reflection--
absorption equals emission.

01:21:13.090 --> 01:21:14.890
That's Kerchhoff's law.

01:21:14.890 --> 01:21:18.940
So this gives you now
the value that you will

01:21:18.940 --> 01:21:22.330
see that you can appreciate.

01:21:22.330 --> 01:21:24.650
OK?

01:21:24.650 --> 01:21:26.500
We'll continue next lecture.

